CLASS:: SwarmInstrument
summary:: Select named spectral definitions around one SwarmMath state
categories:: Libraries>SwarmSynth
related:: Classes/SwarmMath, Classes/SwarmSynth

DESCRIPTION::
SwarmInstrument keeps named timbre variants separate from score scheduling. A variant replaces the state's complete spectral argument dictionary and may provide default partial and variation counts. Pitch, volume, output routing, duration, and gate values remain attached to the existing state.

The term code::variant:: means a named timbre definition. link::Classes/SwarmMath:: code::variations:: continues to mean multiple generated voices per partial.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: synthDef
The single SynthDef used by this instrument.
argument:: state
The SwarmMath instance whose identity is retained.
argument:: variants
A nonempty dictionary mapping symbols to definitions. Each definition contains a complete code::args:: dictionary and optional code::partials:: and code::variations:: counts. If one variant omits a control used by another, its neutral value must exist in code::defaultParams:: or the registered SynthDesc; construction fails rather than guessing a value.
argument:: variant
The selected definition, initially code::\original::.
argument:: defaultParams
Default controls forwarded to a lazily created SwarmSynth.
argument:: hasGate
Forwarded to SwarmSynth.
argument:: liveSwitch
code::\sustained:: updates active nodes. code::\nextTrigger:: leaves active nodes unchanged until the next play call.
argument:: synth
An optional borrowed playback object. If omitted, SwarmSynth is created on first playback and owned by this wrapper.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: variantNames
Returns the sorted available names.

METHOD:: variants
Returns a defensive copy. Editing it cannot change registered definitions.

METHOD:: variant
Returns the selected name. Assigning a name performs an immediate switch.

METHOD:: state
Returns the retained SwarmMath state.

METHOD:: synth
Returns the playback object, or nil before lazy construction.

METHOD:: setVariant
Selects a definition atomically.
argument:: name
Registered variant name.
argument:: transitionTime
Zero updates sustained playback immediately. A positive value linearly transitions to one sampled target.
argument:: preserveDimensions
When true, retain the state's current partial and variation counts instead of applying counts stored in the variant.
argument:: applyLive
When false, update selection and state without touching active playback. This is useful when a cue applies a preset separately.

Existing nodes retain phase and pan. Added nodes receive the new definition normally. A new switch cancels an earlier transition.

All generated ratios and frequencies, and numeric amplitudes, are validated before selection is committed. Validation-only sampling for idle and next-trigger instruments restores the random stream; active sustained switches reuse their one sampled target during playback.

METHOD:: reapplyVariant
Restores the currently selected definition after runtime timbre edits without changing its name. By default this preserves dimensions and does not touch active playback, which lets cue code restore a preset before issuing its existing playback update. Optional live application follows the same transition rules as code::setVariant::.

METHOD:: cloneStateForVariant
Returns an independent SwarmMath copy for inspection or private audition. It does not change selection or playback.

METHOD:: bind
Rebinds state and playback references without applying the selected definition. This supports composition registries whose globals may be replaced during live coding.

METHOD:: play
Applies an Event through SwarmMath pitch resolution, creates owned playback if necessary, and delegates playback. Duration and gate scheduling remain the caller's responsibility.

METHOD:: closeGate
Cancels transitions and closes active gates.

METHOD:: release
Cancels transitions and releases playback nodes.

METHOD:: dispose
Cancels transitions and disposes only playback created by this wrapper. Borrowed playback remains owned by its caller.

EXAMPLES::

code::
(
var variants = (
    original: (args: (
        freq: { |e| e.freq * e.p1 },
        amp: { |e| e.vol / e.p1 }, phase: { 0 }, pan: { 0 }
    ), partials: 12, variations: 1),
    revised: (args: (
        ratio: { |e| e.p1 ** 1.08 },
        freq: { |e| SwarmMath.freqRatio(e) },
        amp: { |e| SwarmMath.ampPower(e, 2) * e.vol },
        phase: { 0 }, pan: { 0 }
    ), partials: 12, variations: 1)
);

~voice = SwarmInstrument.new(\swarm_partial,
    SwarmMath.new([110], 12, 1, variants[\original][\args], 0.08),
    variants, variant: \original);
~voice.play((midinote: 45));
~voice.setVariant(\revised, transitionTime: 0.5, preserveDimensions: true);
~voice.closeGate;
~voice.dispose;
)
::
